// ===================================================================================================================================
// File          : PlaywrightFactory.java
// Package       : commonFunctions
// Description   : Owns the Playwright object graph for the BISS automation framework.
//                   Playwright  ->  Browser  ->  BrowserContext  ->  Page
//                 One graph per thread (ThreadLocal) because Playwright objects are NOT thread-safe.
//                 Replaces the Selenium WebDriver / WebDriverWait ThreadLocals that lived in CommonFunctions.
//
//                 Container-first design:
//                   - headless by default under the docker profile, fixed 1920x1080 viewport
//                   - no driver binaries, no chromedriver.exe
//                   - leftover browser processes stopped before launch on the laptop only (BrowserProcessCleaner)
//                   - browsers come from the image (PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH), never downloaded at run time
//                   - every BrowserContext is already isolated (equivalent of Chrome --incognito + temp profile)
//                   - Playwright trace (.zip) recorded per test case and kept on failure for offline debugging
//
// Config keys (application*.properties, -D or BISS_ env var):
//   headless                       true | false
//   browser.channel                blank (bundled Chromium) | chrome | msedge  (set = no browser download)
//   playwright.skip.browser.download   true = never download browsers (laptops behind the web gateway)
//   viewport.width / viewport.height   default 1920 / 1080
//   browser.maximize               true = headed window uses full screen size (local runs only)
//   browser.zoom.percent           page zoom, same as Ctrl+minus in Chrome (default 100; e.g. 67, 70, 80)
//   explicit.wait.seconds          default action timeout
//   page.load.timeout.seconds      default navigation timeout
//   playwright.slowmo.ms           slow motion for demos (default 0)
//   ignore.https.errors            accept self-signed / internal CA certificates
//   browser.proxy.server           e.g. http://proxy.agriculture.gov.ie:8080 (blank = none)
//   browser.proxy.bypass           e.g. *.agriculture.gov.ie
//   browser.locale / browser.timezone   default en-IE / Europe/Dublin
//   trace.mode                     off | on | retain-on-failure
//   log.browser.events             true = log page changes, new tabs, pop-up dialogs, failed requests and HTTP errors
//   log.browser.console.errors     true = also log JavaScript console errors from the application
//   browser.https.upgrades         true = http:// links are opened over https:// first, like normal Chrome (default true)
//   browser.https.upgrade.hosts    optional list of hosts always sent from http:// to https:// (e.g. agfood.icentest.agriculture.gov.ie)
//   dialog.default.action          accept | dismiss - what to do with alert / confirm / prompt pop-ups (default accept)
//                                  'Leave site?' (beforeunload) pop-ups are always accepted, as Selenium does
//   browser.cleanup.before.start   none | automation | all - browser processes stopped before launch (BrowserProcessCleaner)
//   browser.cleanup.temp.folders   true = delete old Playwright temp folders once per run
//   report.traces.path             default Test_Report/traces
//   report.downloads.path          every downloaded file is saved here (default Test_Report/downloads)
//   report.downloads.path          default Test_Report/downloads
//
// Page zoom (browser.zoom.percent):
//   Chrome / Chromium / Edge : the zoom is written into a fresh temporary browser profile as Chrome's own
//                              default zoom preference, exactly what the Selenium framework did with
//                              profile.default_zoom_level = -2.196545 (67%). The page gets the wider layout,
//                              clicks and screenshots keep working, and the profile is deleted afterwards.
//                              Headless runs without browser.channel use channel 'chromium' (full browser in new
//                              headless mode), because the default headless shell ignores the zoom preference.
//   Firefox / WebKit         : no such preference, so a CSS zoom on the page root is used instead.
//
// Author        : Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@goverment.ie
// Date Created  : 15-09-2026
// Updated       : 16-09-2026 - browser.zoom.percent (real Chrome page zoom through the profile preference)
// Updated       : 16-09-2026 - Browser event log (page changes, new tabs, dialogs, failed requests) and dialog handling
// Updated       : 16-09-2026 - Chrome HTTPS-Upgrades switched back on (Exit link to http://agfood... timed out on port 80)
// Updated       : 17-09-2026 - browser.chromium.sandbox (removes the --no-sandbox banner on the laptop)
// Updated       : 17-09-2026 - Leftover Chrome / driver processes and temp folders cleaned before launch (browser.cleanup.*)
// Updated       : 18-09-2026 - Every file the application downloads is saved under report.downloads.path and listed
//                              by getDownloads() (the browser in a container has no Windows Downloads folder)
// ===================================================================================================================================

